}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For each of the sixteen Boolean words u of length six that begin and end in \
black, and every r>=74, no column of a configuration with a leftmost black \
cell eventually repeats ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"0", "^", "r"}], " ", "u"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 ". The transient, column, and initial configuration size are unrestricted. \
This includes every column of every nonzero finite starting configuration and \
the single-seed center."
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The formal headline in ",
 StyleBox["this notebook source",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Rule30Submission", ".", "no_six"}], "_bit", "_core"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 ". Its hypothesis is membership in the explicitly listed sixteen cores. The \
modular catalog separately combines these results with the earlier five-tail \
proof and a rotation/decomposition theorem to cover ",
 StyleBox["all",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " tails of length at most six. That larger wrapper is not claimed as a \
theorem of the standalone environment embedded here."
}], "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],

Cell["\<\
Some concrete words overlap earlier certificates. Global novelty is not \
established. No full Rule 30 Prize problem is solved, and the alternating \
period remains open.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sixCoreWords", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"IntegerString", "[", 
      RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"33", ",", " ", "63", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Grid", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Partition", "[", 
    RowBox[{"sixCoreWords", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "All"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->774702189,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {"\<\"100001\"\>", "\<\"100011\"\>", "\<\"100101\"\>", "\<\"100111\"\>"},
    {"\<\"101001\"\>", "\<\"101011\"\>", "\<\"101101\"\>", "\<\"101111\"\>"},
    {"\<\"110001\"\>", "\<\"110011\"\>", "\<\"110101\"\>", "\<\"110111\"\>"},
    {"\<\"111001\"\>", "\<\"111011\"\>", "\<\"111101\"\>", "\<\"111111\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[3]= ",
 CellID->2112754412,ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["A finite obstruction proves infinitely many exclusions", "Section",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],

Cell["\<\
The earlier white-pulse theorem forces a hypothetical periodic column's right \
neighbor to be white during the early part of its long white run. A nearby \
black cell would reach that neighbor too soon. Consequently a sufficiently \
wide strip must be entirely white at every period start.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Start at that all-white endpoint and calculate predecessor sets backward, \
allowing both right-boundary inputs at every step. If the predecessor set \
becomes empty after the tail and N preceding white steps, no actual strip can \
realize that block. The generic backward-vacuum theorem then excludes every \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"0", "^", "r"}], " ", "u"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],
 " with"
}], "Text",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "    r >= max(N, 10",
 StyleBox["length(u)+11, K+9", "TI"],
 "(length(u)+1))."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell["\<\
This does not extrapolate from finitely many padding lengths. The fixed \
terminal block is present in every longer white-padded word, while the \
analytic theorem supplies the all-white endpoint for every sufficiently large \
r.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the basic six-bit certificates, width fourteen is sufficient and the \
common bound is 77. The largest case, ",
 Cell[BoxData["110001"], "InlineFormula",
