Cell["Endpoint refinements give the bound 74", "Section",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],

Cell["\<\
Two smaller endpoint-conditioned calculations sharpen the common bound. They \
retain only white-phase states in a closed white-driven set, intersect \
backward predecessors with forward tail states, and force the neighboring bit \
at every white phase. The effective OR boundary would therefore be periodic, \
contrary to the uniform masked Jen theorem.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData["110001"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],
 " refinement uses width twelve and fourteen backward white steps; its \
analytic width bound is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"12", "-", "1", "+", 
    RowBox[{"9", "*", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"6", "+", "1"}], ")"}]}]}], "=", "74"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 ". The ",
 Cell[BoxData["111101"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 " refinement uses width ten and gives the sufficient bound 72. Every other \
six-bit core already has a bound at most 74, so the common sixteen-core bound \
is 74. No optimality is claimed."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],

Cell["Independent computations", "Section",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell["\<\
A cellwise Boolean implementation independently reconstructed every basic \
predecessor set, covering 889,216 transition cases. Three negative controls \
retain vacuum predecessors. A second cellwise check validates the endpoint \
sets, forward images, and forced bits, and rejects an incorrect terminal bit.\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Wolfram's free remote evaluator (15.0.1) independently encoded all sixteen \
basic finite obstructions as Boolean satisfiability problems. Every positive \
case was UNSAT; removing one required white step from the largest case was \
SAT. The exact code and returned outputs are archived under ",
 Cell["evidence/wolfram/", "InlineCode",ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 ". These are exploratory Wolfram computations, not a prize-verifier \
verdict."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],

Cell["Formal proof", "Section",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The following cell embeds every research dependency of the sixteen-core \
proof. It imports only modules already present in the pinned kit, plus the \
required ",
 Cell[BoxData["Rule30PrizeKit"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 " root. It does not depend on files from an unmerged contribution branch. \
The modular proof and local kernel-check reports are supplied separately."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell["\<\
The Wolfram/LeanLink cells evaluate the included proof and display the \
module's kernel replay below. A successful local replay checks every \
declaration of that module. The prize verifier evaluates the notebook again \
after submission.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`LeanLink`\>\"", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$Rule30PrizeKit", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Environment", "[", "\"\<RULE30PRIZE_KIT\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"If", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"!", 
      RowBox[{"StringQ", "[", "$Rule30PrizeKit", "]"}]}], " ", "||", " ", 
     RowBox[{"!", 
      RowBox[{"DirectoryQ", "[", "$Rule30PrizeKit", "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Abort", "[", "]"}]}], "]"}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rule30Submission", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"LeanImportString", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<import Rule30PrizeKit\\nimport \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30FiniteBlackRuns\\nimport \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30LightCone\\nimport \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30StripCertificates\\nimport \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30FiniteMaskedJen\\n\\n/- Source: \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30FiniteStripsResearch -/\\n/-!\\n# Bitmask \
strip certificates for arbitrary left-finite configurations\\n\\nThe \
certificate checker has no initial-state dependence. Its soundness \
extends\\nfrom the single seed to every column of any configuration with a \
leftmost\\nblack cell, by the existing uniform masked Jen theorem. In \
particular every\\nconcrete bitmask certificate in the catalog has this \
stronger conclusion.\\n-/\\n\\nnamespace \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata\\nnamespace Rule30FiniteStripsResearch\\n\\nopen \
Rule30Jen Rule30Realization Rule30FiniteConfigs \
Rule30StripCertificates\\n\\n/-- Column i eventually reads the nonempty word \
w, starting at an arbitrary transient. -/\\ndef EventuallyWord (x : Int \
\[RightArrow] Bool) (i : Int) (w : List Bool) : Prop :=\\n  \[Exists] T, \
\[ForAll] t, T \[LessEqual] t \[RightArrow] evol x t i = w.getD ((t - T) % \
w.length) false\\n\\n/-- Strip encoding: `r < 2 ^ K` and bit `k < K` of `r` \
is `evol x t (j + 1 + k)`. -/\\ndef Enc (x : Int \[RightArrow] Bool) (K t : \
Nat) (j : Int) (r : Nat) : Prop :=\\n  r < 2 ^ K \[And] \[ForAll] k, k < K \
\[RightArrow] r.testBit k = evol x t (j + 1 + k)\\n\\ntheorem enc_step {x : \
Int \[RightArrow] Bool} {K t : Nat} {j : Int} {r : Nat} (h : Enc x K t j r) :\
\\n    Enc x K (t + 1) j (stripStep K (evol x t j) (evol x t (j + 1 + K)) r) \
:= by\\n  refine \:27e8stripStep_lt _ _ _ _, fun k hk => ?_\:27e9\\n  rw \
[testBit_stripStep K _ _ r h.1 k hk]\\n  show _ = rule (evol x t (j + 1 + (k \
: Int) - 1)) (evol x t (j + 1 + k)) (evol x t (j + 1 + k + 1))\\n  have hc : \
r.testBit k = evol x t (j + 1 + k) := h.2 k hk\\n  have hl : (if k = 0 then \
evol x t j else r.testBit (k - 1)) = evol x t (j + 1 + (k : Int) - 1) := \
by\\n    split\\n    \[CenterDot] rename_i h0; subst h0; congr 1; omega\\n    \
\[CenterDot] rename_i h0; rw [h.2 (k - 1) (by omega)]; congr 1; omega\\n  \
have hr : (if k + 1 = K then evol x t (j + 1 + K) else r.testBit (k + 1)) \
=\\n      evol x t (j + 1 + k + 1) := by\\n    split\\n    \[CenterDot] \
rename_i h1; congr 1; omega\\n    \[CenterDot] rename_i h1; rw [h.2 (k + 1) \
(by omega)]; congr 1; omega\\n  rw [hl, hc, hr]\\n\\n/-- The encoding of the \
actual strip. -/\\ndef encRow (x : Int \[RightArrow] Bool) (t : Nat) (j : \
Int) : Nat \[RightArrow] Nat\\n  | 0 => 0\\n  | K + 1 => encRow x t j K ||| \
((evol x t (j + 1 + K)).toNat <<< K)\\n\\ntheorem testBit_encRow {x : Int \
\[RightArrow] Bool} (t : Nat) (j : Int) :\\n    \[ForAll] K k, (encRow x t j \
K).testBit k = (decide (k < K) && evol x t (j + 1 + k))\\n  | 0, k => by simp \
[encRow]\\n  | K + 1, k => by\\n    rw [encRow, Nat.testBit_or, \
testBit_encRow t j K k, Nat.testBit_shiftLeft, testBit_toNat]\\n    by_cases \
hk : k < K\\n    \[CenterDot] simp [hk, show k < K + 1 by omega, show \[Not] \
K \[LessEqual] k by omega]\\n    \[CenterDot] by_cases hk' : k = K\\n      \
\[CenterDot] subst hk'; simp\\n      \[CenterDot] simp [hk, show \[Not] k < K \
+ 1 by omega, show k - K \[NotEqual] 0 by omega]\\n\\ntheorem enc_encRow {x : \
Int \[RightArrow] Bool} (K t : Nat) (j : Int) : Enc x K t j (encRow x t j K) \
:= by\\n  refine \:27e8Nat.lt_pow_two_of_testBit _ fun i hi => ?_, fun k hk \
=> ?_\:27e9\\n  \[CenterDot] rw [testBit_encRow]; simp [show \[Not] i < K by \
omega]\\n  \[CenterDot] rw [testBit_encRow]; simp [hk]\\n\\n/-- **Soundness \
of the strip sets.** If the actual strip is in `S` at time `t` and column `j` \
carries\\nthe word `u` from `t` on, the actual strip at time `t + u.length` \
is in `applyWord K u S`. -/\\ntheorem enc_applyWord {x : Int \[RightArrow] \
Bool} {K : Nat} {j : Int} :\\n    \[ForAll] (u : List Bool) (t r S : Nat), \
Enc x K t j r \[RightArrow] S.testBit r = true \[RightArrow]\\n      (\
\[ForAll] s, s < u.length \[RightArrow] evol x (t + s) j = u.getD s false) \
\[RightArrow]\\n      \[Exists] r', Enc x K (t + u.length) j r' \[And] \
(applyWord K u S).testBit r' = true\\n  | [], t, r, S, he, hS, _ => \:27e8r, \
he, hS\:27e9\\n  | a :: u, t, r, S, he, hS, hu => by\\n    have ha : evol x t \
j = a := by simpa using hu 0 (by simp)\\n    have he1 := enc_step he\\n    rw \
[ha] at he1\\n    have hS1 : (image K a S).testBit (stripStep K a (evol x t \
(j + 1 + K)) r) = true :=\\n      mem_imageAux hS _ (2 ^ K) he.1\\n    obtain \
\:27e8r', he', hS'\:27e9 := enc_applyWord u (t + 1) _ _ he1 hS1 (fun s hs => \
by\\n      have := hu (s + 1) (by simp; omega)\\n      rw [show t + (s + 1) = \
t + 1 + s by omega] at this\\n      simpa using this)\\n    refine \:27e8r', \
?_, hS'\:27e9\\n    rw [show t + (a :: u).length = t + 1 + u.length by simp; \
omega]\\n    exact he'\\n\\ntheorem enc_iterW {x : Int \[RightArrow] Bool} {K \
: Nat} {j : Int} (w : List Bool) :\\n    \[ForAll] (k t r S : Nat), Enc x K t \
j r \[RightArrow] S.testBit r = true \[RightArrow]\\n      (\[ForAll] m s, m \
< k \[RightArrow] s < w.length \[RightArrow] evol x (t + m * w.length + s) j \
= w.getD s false) \[RightArrow]\\n      \[Exists] r', Enc x K (t + k * \
w.length) j r' \[And] (iterW K w k S).testBit r' = true\\n  | 0, t, r, S, he, \
hS, _ => \:27e8r, by simpa using he, hS\:27e9\\n  | k + 1, t, r, S, he, hS, \
hw => by\\n    obtain \:27e8r1, he1, hS1\:27e9 := enc_applyWord w t r S he hS \
(fun s hs => by\\n      simpa using hw 0 s (by omega) hs)\\n    obtain \
\:27e8r', he', hS'\:27e9 := enc_iterW w k (t + w.length) r1 _ he1 hS1 (fun m \
s hm hs => by\\n      rw [show t + w.length + m * w.length + s = t + (m + 1) \
* w.length + s by\\n        rw [Nat.succ_mul]; omega]\\n      exact hw (m + \
1) s (by omega) hs)\\n    refine \:27e8r', ?_, hS'\:27e9\\n    rw [show t + \
(k + 1) * w.length = t + w.length + k * w.length by rw [Nat.succ_mul]; omega]\
\\n    exact he'\\n\\n/-- A bitmask strip certificate forces the effective \
right boundary to be eventually periodic,\\nin the evolution of an arbitrary \
configuration, provided column i reads w eventually. -/\\ntheorem \
orCol_exact_period_of_word_strip {x : Int \[RightArrow] Bool} (i : Int) (w : \
List Bool)\\n    (K k : Nat) (hK : 1 \[LessEqual] K) (hw : 0 < w.length)\\n   \
 (hcert : stripCert w K k = true) (hword : EventuallyWord x i w) :\\n    \
\[Exists] T, \[ForAll] t, T \[LessEqual] t \[RightArrow]\\n      \
Rule30FiniteMaskedJen.orCol x i (t + w.length) = Rule30FiniteMaskedJen.orCol \
x i t := by\\n  obtain \:27e8T, hT\:27e9 := hword\\n  unfold stripCert at \
hcert\\n  rw [Bool.and_eq_true] at hcert\\n  obtain \:27e8hsub, hforce\:27e9 \
:= hcert\\n  have hsub' := allBelow_spec hsub\\n  -- the driver is `w` on \
every period from `T`\\n  have hblock : \[ForAll] m s, s < w.length \
\[RightArrow] evol x (T + m * w.length + s) i = w.getD s false := by\\n    \
intro m s hs\\n    rw [hT _ (by omega), show T + m * w.length + s - T = s + m \
* w.length by omega,\\n      Nat.add_mul_mod_self_right, Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hs]\
\\n  let S0 := iterW K w k (fullSet K)\\n  -- after `k` periods the strip is \
in `S0`\\n  have hstart : \[Exists] r, Enc x K (T + k * w.length) i r \[And] \
S0.testBit r = true := by\\n    have h0 := enc_encRow (x := x) K T i\\n    \
have hfull : (fullSet K).testBit (encRow x T i K) = true := by\\n      unfold \
fullSet; rw [Nat.testBit_two_pow_sub_one]; exact decide_eq_true h0.1\\n    \
exact enc_iterW w k T _ _ h0 hfull (fun m s _ hs => hblock m s hs)\\n  -- and \
it stays in `S0` at every later period start\\n  have hinv : \[ForAll] m, \
\[Exists] r, Enc x K (T + (k + m) * w.length) i r \[And] S0.testBit r = true \
:= by\\n    intro m\\n    induction m with\\n    | zero => simpa using hstart\
\\n    | succ m ih =>\\n      obtain \:27e8r, he, hS\:27e9 := ih\\n      \
obtain \:27e8r', he', hS'\:27e9 := enc_applyWord w _ r S0 he hS (fun s hs => \
by\\n        rw [show T + (k + m) * w.length + s = T + (k + m) * w.length + s \
from rfl]\\n        exact hblock (k + m) s hs)\\n      refine \:27e8r', ?_, \
?_\:27e9\\n      \[CenterDot] have hm : (k + (m + 1)) * w.length = (k + m) * \
w.length + w.length := by\\n          rw [show k + (m + 1) = (k + m) + 1 by \
omega, Nat.succ_mul]\\n        rw [hm, \[LeftArrow] Nat.add_assoc]\\n        \
exact he'\\n      \[CenterDot] have hlt : r' < 2 ^ K := he'.1\\n        have \
:= hsub' r' hlt\\n        rw [hS', Bool.not_true, Bool.false_or] at this\\n   \
     exact this\\n  -- the forced value at each white phase\\n  let g : Nat \
\[RightArrow] Bool := fun \[CurlyPhi] => w.getD \[CurlyPhi] false ||\\n    \
!colConst K (applyWord K (w.take \[CurlyPhi]) S0) false\\n  have hform : \
\[ForAll] t, T + k * w.length \[LessEqual] t \[RightArrow] \
Rule30FiniteMaskedJen.orCol x i t = g ((t - T) % w.length) := by\\n    intro \
t ht\\n    have h\[CurlyPhi] : (t - T) % w.length < w.length := Nat.mod_lt _ \
hw\\n    have hdec : t = T + (k + ((t - T) / w.length - k)) * w.length + (t - \
T) % w.length := by\\n      have hd := Nat.div_add_mod (t - T) w.length\\n    \
  have hq : k \[LessEqual] (t - T) / w.length := (Nat.le_div_iff_mul_le hw).2 \
(by omega)\\n      rw [show k + ((t - T) / w.length - k) = (t - T) / w.length \
by omega, Nat.mul_comm]\\n      omega\\n    obtain \:27e8r, he, hS\:27e9 := \
hinv ((t - T) / w.length - k)\\n    obtain \:27e8r', he', hS'\:27e9 := \
enc_applyWord (w.take ((t - T) % w.length)) _ r S0 he hS\\n      (fun s hs => \
by\\n        rw [List.length_take] at hs\\n        have hs' : s < (t - T) % \
w.length := by omega\\n        rw [hblock _ s (by omega)]\\n        simp \
[List.getD_eq_getElem?_getD, hs'])\\n    rw [List.length_take, \
Nat.min_eq_left (Nat.le_of_lt h\[CurlyPhi]), \[LeftArrow] hdec] at he'\\n    \
have hcell : evol x t (i + 1) = r'.testBit 0 := by\\n      simpa using (he'.2 \
0 (by omega)).symm\\n    unfold Rule30FiniteMaskedJen.orCol g\\n    rw [hT t \
(by omega)]\\n    have hf\[CurlyPhi] := List.all_eq_true.mp hforce ((t - T) % \
w.length) (List.mem_range.mpr h\[CurlyPhi])\\n    cases hw\[CurlyPhi] : \
w.getD ((t - T) % w.length) false\\n    \[CenterDot] rw [hw\[CurlyPhi], \
Bool.false_or] at hf\[CurlyPhi]\\n      simp only [Bool.false_or]\\n      rw \
[hcell]\\n      cases hc0 : colConst K (applyWord K (w.take ((t - T) % \
w.length)) S0) false\\n      \[CenterDot] rw [hc0, Bool.false_or] at hf\
\[CurlyPhi]\\n        have := allBelow_spec hf\[CurlyPhi] r' he'.1\\n        \
rw [hS', Bool.not_true, Bool.false_or, beq_iff_eq] at this\\n        rw \
[this]; rfl\\n      \[CenterDot] have := allBelow_spec hc0 r' he'.1\\n        \
rw [hS', Bool.not_true, Bool.false_or, beq_iff_eq] at this\\n        rw \
[this]; rfl\\n    \[CenterDot] rfl\\n  refine \:27e8T + k * w.length, fun t \
ht => ?_\:27e9\\n  show Rule30FiniteMaskedJen.orCol x i (t + w.length) = \
Rule30FiniteMaskedJen.orCol x i t\\n  rw [hform t ht, hform (t + w.length) \
(by omega), show t + w.length - T = (t - T) + w.length by omega,\\n    \
Nat.add_mod_right]\\n\\n\\n/-- Eventual periodicity version of the \
exact-period implication. -/\\ntheorem orCol_periodic_of_word_strip {x : Int \
\[RightArrow] Bool} (i : Int) (w : List Bool)\\n    (K k : Nat) (hK : 1 \
\[LessEqual] K) (hw : 0 < w.length)\\n    (hcert : stripCert w K k = true) \
(hword : EventuallyWord x i w) :\\n    EventuallyPeriodic \
(Rule30FiniteMaskedJen.orCol x i) := by\\n  obtain \:27e8T, hT\:27e9 := \
orCol_exact_period_of_word_strip i w K k hK hw hcert hword\\n  exact \:27e8T, \
w.length, hw, hT\:27e9\\n\\n/-- **Uniform strip soundness.** Every bitmask \
certificate excludes its word at every column\\nof every configuration having \
a leftmost black cell, for every transient. -/\\ntheorem \
not_eventually_word_strip {x : Int \[RightArrow] Bool} {lo : Int}\\n    (hlo \
: x lo = true) (hzero : \[ForAll] p, p < lo \[RightArrow] x p = false) (i : \
Int)\\n    (w : List Bool) (K k : Nat) (hK : 1 \[LessEqual] K) (hw : 0 < \
w.length)\\n    (hcert : stripCert w K k = true) : \[Not] EventuallyWord x i \
w := by\\n  intro hword\\n  have hcper : EventuallyPeriodic (fun t => evol x \
t i) := by\\n    obtain \:27e8T, hT\:27e9 := hword\\n    refine \:27e8T, \
w.length, hw, fun t ht => ?_\:27e9\\n    change evol x (t + w.length) i = \
evol x t i\\n    rw [hT t ht, hT (t + w.length) (by omega),\\n      show t + \
w.length - T = (t - T) + w.length by omega, Nat.add_mod_right]\\n  exact \
Rule30FiniteMaskedJen.orCol_not_eventuallyPeriodic hlo hzero i hcper\\n    \
(orCol_periodic_of_word_strip i w K k hK hw hcert hword)\\n\\n/-- In \
particular, the certificate excludes the word in every column of every \
nonzero finite\\nconfiguration. Neither the column nor the transient is \
bounded. -/\\ntheorem not_eventually_word_strip_finite {x : Int \[RightArrow] \
Bool}\\n    (hfin : Rule30PeriodTwoSideways.FinConfig x) (hne : \[Exists] p, \
x p = true) (i : Int)\\n    (w : List Bool) (K k : Nat) (hK : 1 \[LessEqual] \
K) (hw : 0 < w.length)\\n    (hcert : stripCert w K k = true) : \[Not] \
EventuallyWord x i w := by\\n  obtain \:27e8lo, hlo, hzero\:27e9 := \
exists_leftmost hfin hne\\n  exact not_eventually_word_strip hlo hzero i w K \
k hK hw hcert\\n\\n\\nend Rule30FiniteStripsResearch\\nend \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata\\n\\n/- Source: \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30WhitePulseResearch -/\\n/-!\\n# A shield \
survives every short pulse\\n\\nA black run in the first right column creates \
a striped block. An interior black\\ncell of that block survives an arbitrary \
boundary pulse of length m by locality.\\nThese lemmas quantify the \
absorbing, synchronized regime without enumerating tails.\\nThey do not prove \
every periodic history enters that regime.\\n-/\\nnamespace \
Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30WhitePulseResearch\\nopen Rule30Jen \
Rule30Realization Rule30FiniteBlackRuns Rule30ZeroBoundaryBarriers\\n\\n/-- A \
spatially stationary stripe, black at odd offsets from column i. -/\\ndef \
stripe (i p : Int) : Bool := decide ((p - i) % 2 = 1)\\n\\ntheorem \
stripe_step (i p : Int) :\\n    rule (stripe i (p - 1)) (stripe i p) (stripe \
i (p + 1)) = stripe i p := by\\n  have hp : (p - i) % 2 = 0 \[Or] (p - i) % 2 \
= 1 := by omega\\n  rcases hp with hp | hp\\n  \[CenterDot] have hl : (p - 1 \
- i) % 2 = 1 := by omega\\n    have hr : (p + 1 - i) % 2 = 1 := by omega\\n   \
 simp [stripe, rule, hp, hl, hr]\\n  \[CenterDot] have hl : (p - 1 - i) % 2 = \
0 := by omega\\n    have hr : (p + 1 - i) % 2 = 0 := by omega\\n    simp \
[stripe, rule, hp, hl, hr]\\n\\ntheorem evol_stripe (i : Int) : \[ForAll] t \
p, evol (stripe i) t p = stripe i p\\n  | 0, p => rfl\\n  | t+1, p => by\\n   \
 change rule (evol (stripe i) t (p-1)) (evol (stripe i) t p)\\n      (evol \
(stripe i) t (p+1)) = stripe i p\\n    rw [evol_stripe i t (p-1), evol_stripe \
i t p, evol_stripe i t (p+1), stripe_step]\\n\\n/-- The nine-black shield is \
a whole stripe on its forced interval. -/\\ntheorem shield_stripe (x : Int \
\[RightArrow] Bool) (i : Int) (a j : Nat)\\n    (hblack : \[ForAll] s, s < \
9*j \[RightArrow] evol x (a+s) (i+1) = true)\\n    (p : Int) (hlo : i+2 \
\[LessEqual] p) (hhi : p \[LessEqual] i+2*j+1) :\\n    evol x (a+9*j) p = \
stripe i p := by\\n  have hs := black_shield x (i+1) j a hblack\\n  let k : \
Nat := ((p-i)/2).toNat\\n  have hk : (k : Int) = (p-i)/2 := by\\n    dsimp \
[k]\\n    exact Int.toNat_of_nonneg (by omega)\\n  have hklo : 1 \[LessEqual] \
k := by omega\\n  have hkhi : k \[LessEqual] j := by omega\\n  have hp : \
(p-i)%2 = 0 \[Or] (p-i)%2 = 1 := by omega\\n  rcases hp with hp | hp\\n  \
\[CenterDot] have he : p = (i+1)+2*(k:Int)-1 := by omega\\n    rw [he, (hs k \
hklo hkhi).1]\\n    simp [stripe, show ((i+1)+2*(k:Int)-1-i)%2 = 0 by \
omega]\\n  \[CenterDot] have he : p = (i+1)+2*(k:Int) := by omega\\n    rw \
[he, (hs k hklo hkhi).2]\\n    simp [stripe, show ((i+1)+2*(k:Int)-i)%2 = 1 \
by omega]\\n\\n/-- **An arbitrary m-step pulse cannot erase the entire \
shield.** After 9(m+1) black steps\\nof column i+1, a black cell survives any \
following m steps at an explicitly bounded distance.\\nThere is no hypothesis \
on the boundary column during those m steps. -/\\ntheorem \
black_survives_pulse (x : Int \[RightArrow] Bool) (i : Int) (a m : Nat)\\n    \
(hblack : \[ForAll] s, s < 9*(m+1) \[RightArrow] evol x (a+s) (i+1) = true) :\
\\n    evol x (a+9*(m+1)+m) (i+(2*(m/2)+3 : Nat)) = true := by\\n  let q : \
Nat := 2*(m/2)+3\\n  have hqlo : m+2 \[LessEqual] q := by dsimp [q]; omega\\n \
 have hqhi : q \[LessEqual] m+3 := by dsimp [q]; omega\\n  have hloc := \
Rule30LightCone.evol_window (x := stripe i)\\n    (x' := fun p => evol x \
(a+9*(m+1)) p) (t := m) (p := i+q)\\n    (fun p hp1 hp2 => shield_stripe x i \
a (m+1) hblack p (by omega) (by omega))\\n  rw [evol_restart, evol_stripe] at \
hloc\\n  rw [hloc]\\n  simp only [stripe, decide_eq_true_eq]\\n  dsimp [q]\\n \
 omega\\n\\n/-- During n white boundary steps, any black cell initially n+1 \
places to the right forces\\ncolumn i+1 to be black by the end. No assumption \
is needed on the intervening cells. -/\\ntheorem black_reaches_boundary (x : \
Int \[RightArrow] Bool) : \[ForAll] (n : Nat) (i : Int) (a : Nat),\\n    (\
\[ForAll] s, s < n \[RightArrow] evol x (a+s) i = false) \[RightArrow]\\n    \
evol x a (i+(n+1 : Nat)) = true \[RightArrow] evol x (a+n) (i+1) = true\\n  | \
0, i, a, _, hb => by simpa using hb\\n  | n+1, i, a, hw, hb => by\\n    cases \
hf : evol x (a+(n+1)) (i+1)\\n    \[CenterDot] have h1 : \[ForAll] s, s \
\[LessEqual] n+1 \[RightArrow] evol x (a+s) (i+1) = false := by\\n        \
intro s hs\\n        cases hb1 : evol x (a+s) (i+1)\\n        \[CenterDot] \
rfl\\n        \[CenterDot] have hm := Rule30FiniteBlackRuns.black_stays x i \
(a+s) (n+1-s)\\n            (fun k hk => by\\n              have hh := hw \
(s+k) (by omega)\\n              rwa [show a+(s+k) = (a+s)+k by omega] at hh)\
\\n            hb1 (n+1-s) (Nat.le_refl _)\\n          rw [show a+s+(n+1-s) = \
a+(n+1) by omega, hf] at hm\\n          exact absurd hm (by decide)\\n      \
have hb' : evol x a ((i+1)+(n+1 : Nat)) = true := by\\n        rw [show \
(i+1)+((n+1 : Nat) : Int) = i+((n+1+1 : Nat) : Int) by omega]\\n        exact \
hb\\n      have ih := black_reaches_boundary x n (i+1) a (fun s hs => h1 s \
(by omega)) hb'\\n      have hstep : evol x (a+(n+1)) (i+1) =\\n          \
rule (evol x (a+n) i) (evol x (a+n) (i+1)) (evol x (a+n) (i+2)) := by\\n      \
  rw [show a+(n+1) = (a+n)+1 by omega]\\n        change rule (evol x (a+n) \
(i+1-1)) (evol x (a+n) (i+1))\\n          (evol x (a+n) (i+1+1)) = _\\n       \
 congr 2 <;> omega\\n      rw [hw n (by omega), h1 n (by omega),\\n        \
show i+2 = (i+1)+1 by omega, ih, hf] at hstep\\n      exact absurd hstep (by \
decide)\\n    \[CenterDot] rfl\\n\\n/-- **One absorbing step.** Once a white \
interval has a sufficiently early black neighbour,\\nany following m-step \
pulse leaves a black cell close enough that the next white interval\\nhas a \
black neighbour after at most m+2 steps. The pulse is entirely arbitrary. \
-/\\ntheorem white_pulse_return (x : Int \[RightArrow] Bool) (i : Int) (a r m \
s : Nat)\\n    (hw : \[ForAll] k, k < r \[RightArrow] evol x (a+k) i = false)\
\\n    (hearly : evol x (a+s) (i+1) = true) (hs : s+9*(m+1) \[LessEqual] \
r)\\n    (hnext : \[ForAll] k, k < r \[RightArrow] evol x (a+r+m+k) i = \
false) :\\n    \[ForAll] k, m+2 \[LessEqual] k \[RightArrow] k \[LessEqual] r \
\[RightArrow] evol x (a+r+m+k) (i+1) = true := by\\n  have hhold := \
Rule30FiniteBlackRuns.black_stays x i (a+s) (r-s)\\n    (fun k hk => by\\n    \
  have hh := hw (s+k) (by omega)\\n      rwa [show a+(s+k) = (a+s)+k by \
omega] at hh) hearly\\n  have hlast : \[ForAll] k, k < 9*(m+1) \[RightArrow] \
evol x (a+r-9*(m+1)+k) (i+1) = true := by\\n    intro k hk\\n    have hh := \
hhold (r-9*(m+1)-s+k) (by omega)\\n    rwa [show a+s+(r-9*(m+1)-s+k) = \
a+r-9*(m+1)+k by omega] at hh\\n  have hsurv := black_survives_pulse x i \
(a+r-9*(m+1)) m hlast\\n  rw [show a+r-9*(m+1)+9*(m+1)+m = a+r+m by omega] at \
hsurv\\n  let q : Nat := 2*(m/2)+3\\n  have hqlo : 1 \[LessEqual] q := by \
dsimp [q]; omega\\n  have hqhi : q-1 \[LessEqual] m+2 := by dsimp [q]; \
omega\\n  have hqr : q-1 \[LessEqual] r := by omega\\n  have harr := \
black_reaches_boundary x (q-1) i (a+r+m)\\n    (fun k hk => hnext k (by \
omega)) (by simpa only [show q-1+1 = q by omega] using hsurv)\\n  have hstay \
:= Rule30FiniteBlackRuns.black_stays x i ((a+r+m)+(q-1)) (r-(q-1))\\n    (fun \
k hk => by\\n      have hh := hnext (q-1+k) (by omega)\\n      rwa [show \
a+r+m+(q-1+k) = ((a+r+m)+(q-1))+k by omega] at hh) harr\\n  intro k hk hkr\\n \
 have hh := hstay (k-(q-1)) (by omega)\\n  rwa [show (a+r+m)+(q-1)+(k-(q-1)) \
= a+r+m+k by omega] at hh\\n\\n/-- **The absorbing regime persists for \
arbitrary pulses.** If every cycle starts with r white\\nsteps, r\
\[GreaterEqual]10m+11, one early black neighbour forces all later white \
intervals to have a black\\nneighbour from phase m+2 on. No periodicity or \
restriction on the m pulse bits is assumed. -/\\ntheorem \
absorbing_white_cycles (x : Int \[RightArrow] Bool) (i : Int) (a r m s : Nat)\
\\n    (hr : 10*m+11 \[LessEqual] r)\\n    (hw : \[ForAll] n k, k < r \
\[RightArrow] evol x (a+n*(r+m)+k) i = false)\\n    (hearly : evol x (a+s) \
(i+1) = true) (hs : s+9*(m+1) \[LessEqual] r) :\\n    \[ForAll] n, 1 \
\[LessEqual] n \[RightArrow] \[ForAll] k, m+2 \[LessEqual] k \[RightArrow] k \
\[LessEqual] r \[RightArrow]\\n      evol x (a+n*(r+m)+k) (i+1) = true := \
by\\n  have hcycle : \[ForAll] n, \[ForAll] k, m+2 \[LessEqual] k \
\[RightArrow] k \[LessEqual] r \[RightArrow]\\n      evol x (a+(n+1)*(r+m)+k) \
(i+1) = true := by\\n    intro n\\n    induction n with\\n    | zero =>\\n    \
  simpa only [Nat.zero_add, Nat.one_mul, Nat.add_assoc] using\\n        \
white_pulse_return x i a r m s (by simpa using hw 0) hearly hs\\n          \
(by simpa [Nat.one_mul, Nat.add_assoc] using hw 1)\\n    | succ n ih =>\\n    \
  have h := white_pulse_return x i (a+(n+1)*(r+m)) r m (m+2)\\n        (hw \
(n+1)) (ih (m+2) (Nat.le_refl _) (by omega)) (by omega)\\n        (fun k hk \
=> by\\n          have hh := hw (n+2) k hk\\n          rwa [show \
a+(n+2)*(r+m)+k = a+(n+1)*(r+m)+r+m+k by\\n            rw [show n+2 = (n+1)+1 \
by omega, Nat.succ_mul]; omega] at hh)\\n      intro k hk hkr\\n      have hh \
:= h k hk hkr\\n      rwa [show a+(n+1)*(r+m)+r+m+k = a+(n+1+1)*(r+m)+k by\\n \
       rw [Nat.succ_mul (n+1) (r+m)]; omega] at hh\\n  intro n hn k hk hkr\\n \
 have hh := hcycle (n-1) k hk hkr\\n  rwa [show n-1+1 = n by omega] at \
hh\\n\\n/-- **Synchronization of the neighbour.** For a periodic boundary \
with r white phases and m\\narbitrary pulse phases, r\[GreaterEqual]10m+11, \
entering the early-black regime forces the entire neighbour\\ncolumn to be \
eventually periodic. This statement is independent of the initial \
configuration. -/\\ntheorem periodic_neighbour_of_early_black (x : Int \
\[RightArrow] Bool) (i : Int) (a r m s : Nat)\\n    (hr : 10*m+11 \
\[LessEqual] r)\\n    (hper : \[ForAll] t, a \[LessEqual] t \[RightArrow] \
evol x (t+(r+m)) i = evol x t i)\\n    (hw : \[ForAll] n k, k < r \
\[RightArrow] evol x (a+n*(r+m)+k) i = false)\\n    (hearly : evol x (a+s) \
(i+1) = true) (hs : s+9*(m+1) \[LessEqual] r) :\\n    EventuallyPeriodic (fun \
t => evol x t (i+1)) := by\\n  let b : Nat \[RightArrow] Nat := fun n => \
a+(n+1)*(r+m)+r\\n  have hb (n : Nat) : b (n+1) = b n+(r+m) := by\\n    dsimp \
[b]\\n    rw [Nat.succ_mul (n+1) (r+m)]\\n    omega\\n  have hbounds (n : \
