\\n# A finite vacuum-avoidance criterion for arbitrary white-padding families\
\\n\\nA stable zero-driven reachable set G and the single finite check that a \
pulse u\\ncannot send G to the vacuum imply exclusions of 0^r u for all \
sufficiently large r.\\nThe length and contents of u are unrestricted. This \
does not establish that such\\nvacuum-avoidance certificates exist for every \
pulse.\\n-/\\nnamespace \
